      "content": "To effectively challenge Democratic Socialism, focus the debate on the inherent conflict between strong central planning and individual economic freedom. A core argument is that the state control necessary for socialist goals invariably leads to bureaucratic overreach, stifling the innovation and dynamism that drive capitalist success. You can also highlight the practical issue of how large, state-funded social safety nets are often financed, suggesting that the necessary tax increases can inevitably lead to disincentivizing the very hard work required to support the system.",
